WEBVTT

00:16.474 --> 00:17.851
Did he try to break it for you?

01:22.123 --> 01:24.625
Your soldiers are loyal to you.

01:24.626 --> 01:26.960
I think they're worried
we're gonna execute you.

01:26.961 --> 01:29.546
If I was getting executed,
Isaac would've come himself.

01:29.547 --> 01:32.382
There was a shooting near the borderline
between us and the Scars.

01:32.383 --> 01:35.177
Treaty might be broken.
He's dealing with that now.

01:35.178 --> 01:37.179
If it's war again,
we're gonna need all the soldiers we have.

01:37.180 --> 01:40.475
So he's wondering why you apparently
killed some of your own men.

01:42.227 --> 01:43.645
Including Leon.

01:45.897 --> 01:46.898
Leon?

01:49.025 --> 01:50.026
Leon.

01:51.361 --> 01:52.362
Jesus.

01:57.325 --> 01:58.409
What happened?

02:02.831 --> 02:05.499
- My unit is responsible for--
- Securing the hospital.

02:05.500 --> 02:08.795
I know your orders. I gave them, Elise.
What happened?

02:13.174 --> 02:15.426
We cleared the ground floor
up to the sixth.

02:16.553 --> 02:19.305
A few scattered infected here or there.
Nothing we couldn't handle.

02:19.806 --> 02:21.598
All that was left was the basement.

02:21.599 --> 02:23.308
B1, B2, B3.

02:23.309 --> 02:26.103
We were expecting the worst,
the kind of environment they like.

02:26.104 --> 02:27.813
Plus, the old-timers said that down there

02:27.814 --> 02:30.774
was where they brought
the first Cordyceps patients in '03.

02:30.775 --> 02:32.735
On top of that, we had an access problem.

02:34.070 --> 02:38.031
These stairwells here,
here, and here caved in

02:38.032 --> 02:40.033
and all the elevator cars
were stuck in their shafts

02:40.034 --> 02:41.451
just below ground level.

02:41.452 --> 02:44.747
The only way in or out of the basement
is here, this stairwell.

02:46.040 --> 02:48.877
So yesterday,
that's where I sent a squad, down to B1.

02:49.878 --> 02:51.421
- And?
- Nothing.

02:52.422 --> 02:54.299
The whole floor was empty, not even rats.

02:55.091 --> 02:59.052
So today, B2, hoping for more of the same,
I sent another squad down

02:59.053 --> 03:01.306
and I put Leon in charge 'cause

03:04.267 --> 03:05.476
he's my best.

03:08.021 --> 03:09.897
A few minutes in, he radios back.

03:09.898 --> 03:12.191
There's Cordyceps on the walls, the floor.

03:12.192 --> 03:15.944
Chances are, they'll find infected next,
but that's what they were down there for

03:15.945 --> 03:17.738
so I told him to proceed.

03:17.739 --> 03:19.740
Five minutes later, he radios again.

03:19.741 --> 03:21.117
This time, he...

03:24.621 --> 03:26.080
he was struggling to breathe.

03:27.916 --> 03:29.083
He could hardly talk.

03:32.921 --> 03:35.965
I thought maybe he had been bit.

03:37.175 --> 03:39.427
I said, "Leon, were you bit?" He said...

03:42.138 --> 03:43.514
He said, "It's in the air."

03:47.185 --> 03:48.937
He said, "It's in the air.

03:50.313 --> 03:51.397
Seal us in."

03:56.694 --> 03:58.070
And I knew it wasn't in the vents

03:58.071 --> 04:00.113
or we would've all
been infected weeks ago.

04:00.114 --> 04:03.700
So, I scrambled my other team
and we locked the only door to B2

04:03.701 --> 04:05.495
and we locked the only door to B1.

04:06.871 --> 04:08.289
And we did what Leon said.

04:11.584 --> 04:12.919
We sealed them in.

04:18.633 --> 04:20.593
Nothing else has gotten out?

04:21.844 --> 04:23.346
No one else has gotten sick?

04:25.390 --> 04:26.474
Okay.

04:27.475 --> 04:29.852
The hospital's a resource
we can't afford to lose.

04:32.522 --> 04:35.607
I'll inform only the people who absolutely
need to know, and no one else.

04:35.608 --> 04:37.693
As far as I'm concerned, Sergeant Park,

04:37.694 --> 04:41.072
you resolved the situation
permanently and heroically.

04:42.657 --> 04:44.284
We owe you a debt.

04:54.127 --> 04:55.962
I'm sorry about your son.

06:26.302 --> 06:29.262
Patrol 14 heading north
to 13th and Bradford.

06:29.263 --> 06:30.889
One mile out.

06:30.890 --> 06:32.891
One mile out. Copy.

06:32.892 --> 06:34.602
Mobile three.

06:35.311 --> 06:36.437
Mobile three.

06:42.652 --> 06:45.446
Possible movement
at the convention center.

06:50.910 --> 06:52.661
- What?
- Lights.

06:52.662 --> 06:54.246
Oh, good.

06:54.247 --> 06:57.375
They have a big-ass generator down there.
Natural gas, baby.

06:59.877 --> 07:02.129
- You figure it out yet?
- Gettin' there.

07:02.130 --> 07:04.799
You'll find a safe way to get us
to the hospital though, right?

07:12.306 --> 07:13.474
Can I help?

07:14.892 --> 07:16.059
No.

07:16.060 --> 07:17.894
Why, because I'm stupid?

07:17.895 --> 07:19.229
That's not the word I would use.

07:19.230 --> 07:20.565
Really? What word then?

07:22.066 --> 07:23.275
Non-school-oriented.

07:23.276 --> 07:25.486
Fuck you, I went to school. Let me help.

07:28.906 --> 07:31.116
I'm triangulating.

07:31.117 --> 07:32.909
- Do you know how that works?
- Yes.

07:32.910 --> 07:34.287
With triangles.

07:35.580 --> 07:36.746
It's pretty standard.

07:36.747 --> 07:40.500
I get a bearing of their troop movements,
and then triangulate back to their bases.

07:40.501 --> 07:42.043
I'm estimating angles, though.

07:42.044 --> 07:44.421
I mean, if I had a protractor,
it would be a lot more accurate.

07:44.422 --> 07:46.423
Oh, I actually brought a protractor.

07:46.424 --> 07:48.134
- You did?
- No.

07:48.759 --> 07:50.510
I don't know what that is,
and I hated math.

07:50.511 --> 07:52.387
I'm gonna leave you alone now
and go and explore

07:52.388 --> 07:54.723
the rest of this place,
because you're smart as fuck

07:54.724 --> 07:56.058
and you're figuring it out.

07:58.144 --> 08:00.563
- Ellie.
- Yes?

09:58.472 --> 10:01.851
If I ever were to lose you

10:32.131 --> 10:33.466
Did you figure it out?

10:34.508 --> 10:36.385
I think so, yeah.

10:37.553 --> 10:38.554
Good.

10:39.722 --> 10:43.141
We follow a safe path west
until this spot.

10:43.142 --> 10:45.353
Here, let me show you.

10:46.520 --> 10:50.190
They run a line of patrols
north and south, like this.

10:50.191 --> 10:54.361
They're pretty evenly spread out,
so they're watching that entire area.

10:54.362 --> 10:57.072
But there's a gap between here and here.

10:57.073 --> 11:00.076
Now, on this map,
do you see this long-ass building?

11:00.701 --> 11:01.993
Yeah.

11:01.994 --> 11:05.330
So, we cut through and slip by.

11:05.331 --> 11:07.624
What is that long-ass building?

11:07.625 --> 11:09.000
No clue.

11:09.001 --> 11:10.752
But it's set off
from the residential area

11:10.753 --> 11:12.671
so maybe it's a warehouse or something.

11:12.672 --> 11:15.090
It's a big fucking something
for them just to ignore.

11:15.091 --> 11:16.592
Why aren't they patrolling it?

11:18.761 --> 11:21.388
- Infected.
- Probably.

11:21.389 --> 11:25.141
If we make it through,
we pop out behind their patrols.

11:25.142 --> 11:27.977
The hospital's maybe
a quarter mile from there.

11:27.978 --> 11:31.106
Nora should be on the first floor,
far end of the North Wing.

11:31.107 --> 11:32.857
Wait, how the fuck do you know that?

11:32.858 --> 11:34.984
They never shut up. I hear everything.

11:34.985 --> 11:37.237
Morons. Middle of a fucking war

11:37.238 --> 11:38.905
and they're just broadcasting
their positions.

11:38.906 --> 11:40.323
Yeah, so I've been thinking about that.

11:40.324 --> 11:42.575
You know these people
they're fighting, the Scars?

11:42.576 --> 11:44.619
We already know they use
bows and arrows, right?

11:44.620 --> 11:47.580
And they seem culty,
or at least really religious.

11:47.581 --> 11:50.375
- You ever hear of Amish people?
- Amish people? No.

11:50.376 --> 11:53.586
Well, they were around back in '03,
Pennsylvania mostly.

11:53.587 --> 11:55.880
But they chose to live
like it was the 1800s.

11:55.881 --> 11:59.134
Maybe the Scars are like that?
No electricity or technology.

11:59.135 --> 12:02.095
Because these motherfuckers
talk on the radio

12:02.096 --> 12:03.889
like they know no one's listening.

12:04.765 --> 12:07.267
Yeah, and they didn't care
that a walkie was missing.

12:07.268 --> 12:08.935
It's good. They're overconfident.

12:08.936 --> 12:11.063
- It gives us an edge.
- It does.

12:12.189 --> 12:16.193
But what we're doing is reckless,
so kind of a wash.

12:19.655 --> 12:21.322
If we were to leave now,
it'd be dark by the time

12:21.323 --> 12:23.367
we got to the big
fucking something, right?

12:31.834 --> 12:33.294
Let's go be reckless.

12:58.736 --> 13:01.237
Are you sure this way is safe?

13:01.238 --> 13:02.364
You don't trust me?

13:03.365 --> 13:05.241
I trust you. I don't trust Seattle.

13:05.242 --> 13:07.577
Me neither, but let's just talk
like everything's fine

13:07.578 --> 13:09.746
because if I get too anxious,
I'm gonna barf again.

13:09.747 --> 13:11.706
Alright, how 'bout this?

13:11.707 --> 13:13.334
What are you gonna name it?

13:15.711 --> 13:18.172
Oh, if it's a girl, Ellie.

13:18.756 --> 13:20.965
If it's a boy, Elijah.

13:20.966 --> 13:22.592
- Really?
- No.

13:22.593 --> 13:23.928
Why? It's a cool name.

13:25.221 --> 13:26.514
What the fuck?

13:48.828 --> 13:50.411
We shouldn't be here.

13:50.412 --> 13:52.288
We shouldn't have come.
I shouldn't have dragged you here.

13:52.289 --> 13:55.208
You're having a fucking baby.
What am I doing?

13:55.209 --> 13:57.545
Dina, do you wanna go back?

13:58.170 --> 14:00.464
I'll take you back.
You don't need to do this with me.

14:02.716 --> 14:04.552
I'm so fucking stupid.

14:13.269 --> 14:15.771
You know, you never asked me
about the first person I killed.

14:17.523 --> 14:19.191
Okay. Who?

14:20.192 --> 14:25.030
When I was little, we lived in a cabin
in a forest north of Santa Fe.

14:25.531 --> 14:29.702
And there were scattered families around,
but mostly it was just us alone.

14:31.078 --> 14:33.121
And I would get so bored
cooped up with my mom

14:33.122 --> 14:36.165
and sister, I would just beg them,
"Just let me play outside."

14:36.166 --> 14:37.750
But my mom was scared

14:37.751 --> 14:39.837
and she wouldn't let me go outside alone.

14:40.838 --> 14:42.589
But one day, I just fucking did

14:42.590 --> 14:44.424
and I had a gun,
so who's gonna fuck with me?

14:44.425 --> 14:46.426
Now, you already know how this story ends

14:46.427 --> 14:50.388
because I don't live in a cabin
north of Santa Fe anymore

14:50.389 --> 14:52.474
and I don't have a mom or sister anymore.

14:53.183 --> 14:54.851
But since everyone's past is fucked

14:54.852 --> 14:57.020
and we've all heard
everyone's fucked stories,

14:57.021 --> 14:58.522
how do you think this one goes?

14:59.523 --> 15:01.774
I don't know. Raiders?

15:01.775 --> 15:04.278
Just one. And then?

15:05.529 --> 15:09.282
You got home. They were dead, he was gone.

15:09.283 --> 15:11.493
Almost. He was still there.

15:12.536 --> 15:15.413
I heard them screaming
and I ran back with my gun out

15:15.414 --> 15:17.541
but I was too slow
because I was fucking eight.

15:18.125 --> 15:21.128
And when he heard me, he turned around,
and he looked really startled.

15:22.254 --> 15:26.424
And when I shot him,
he looked more startled.

15:26.425 --> 15:30.470
Fuck, I'm so sorry.
I didn't know, I thought...

15:30.471 --> 15:32.389
- How did you get to Jackson?
- It doesn't matter.

15:33.599 --> 15:35.351
This is what matters.

15:36.769 --> 15:39.395
Whatever reason Joel gave those people
to do what they did,

15:39.396 --> 15:41.148
he didn't deserve that.

15:42.024 --> 15:45.486
And I think, what if I hadn't snuck out?

15:46.904 --> 15:50.699
What if my mom and sister
were beaten to death in front of me?

15:51.283 --> 15:53.953
What if that motherfucker
made me watch as he did it?

15:55.329 --> 15:58.290
Would it make a difference if my family
had hurt his people first?

16:00.167 --> 16:01.168
No.

16:03.045 --> 16:04.046
No.

16:05.673 --> 16:07.341
And if I hadn't killed him,

16:08.509 --> 16:10.135
if he had gotten away,

16:11.387 --> 16:14.556
I promise you,
I would have hunted him down forever.

16:16.183 --> 16:17.518
Forever.

16:35.119 --> 16:36.787
I'll go back, if you want.

16:38.747 --> 16:40.708
And I'll keep going, if you want.

16:42.001 --> 16:43.252
There's no right answer.

16:44.044 --> 16:45.587
If I die, it's on me.

16:47.006 --> 16:48.173
It won't be your fault.

16:49.008 --> 16:50.509
So, what do you want to do?

17:02.396 --> 17:03.981
Keep going.

17:29.673 --> 17:31.842
- Do you see anything?
- No. Let's go.

17:41.226 --> 17:42.770
Hurry! Down, down, down.

17:47.357 --> 17:48.567
Cover me.

18:38.992 --> 18:41.035
At least we're not blocked in.

18:41.036 --> 18:42.495
And there are two more positives.

18:42.496 --> 18:45.414
The search lights are up high
to scan the outside,

18:45.415 --> 18:47.416
which means there'll be
no line of sight to the inside.

18:47.417 --> 18:49.837
Good. What's the other positive?

18:51.713 --> 18:55.967
That door's open,
and nothing's come out to kill us, yet.

18:55.968 --> 18:58.137
- Great.
- Maybe.

18:59.429 --> 19:01.931
- I'm gonna take a peek.
- Yeah, you should do that

19:01.932 --> 19:03.684
because you're the one
who can't get infected.

19:16.321 --> 19:17.781
How's it look?

19:20.617 --> 19:22.118
Haunted, but empty.

19:22.119 --> 19:23.954
Oh, just like us.

19:25.497 --> 19:28.249
Look, I'm not saying there won't
be infected somewhere in there.

19:28.250 --> 19:31.169
In fact, there's no fucking way
this entire place is empty.

19:31.170 --> 19:33.505
But simple logic,
it's not gonna be a horde, right?

19:35.966 --> 19:38.050
We're not underground, and the Wolves

19:38.051 --> 19:40.470
are right next door
with their vehicles and lights.

19:41.513 --> 19:42.931
A horde's not gonna ignore that shit.

19:44.183 --> 19:48.936
So what, we've got maybe
a few strays and a couple clickers?

19:48.937 --> 19:51.439
We can handle that.
We've done it like a million times.

19:51.440 --> 19:54.025
Yeah. We'll be okay.

19:54.026 --> 19:56.861
But shooting has to be
a last resort, okay?

19:56.862 --> 19:58.613
Because if the Wolves hear gunfire,

19:58.614 --> 20:00.781
- then we'll have a whole army up our ass.
- Fine.

20:00.782 --> 20:02.075
- Ellie.
- What?

20:03.035 --> 20:05.453
If it gets bad,
and we have to make a choice

20:05.454 --> 20:08.248
between shooting or running, we run.

20:08.832 --> 20:10.334
Last resort, I got it.

20:13.295 --> 20:16.297
Oh, you think that no matter what happens,
I'm just gonna start firing?

20:16.298 --> 20:17.883
Literally every single time. Yes.

20:18.634 --> 20:20.760
Don't get angry. You're a little crazy.

20:20.761 --> 20:23.429
And that's exciting.
It's one of the reasons I love you.

20:23.430 --> 20:25.766
But I do wanna make it out of here.

20:27.559 --> 20:28.810
You love me?

20:36.693 --> 20:38.028
- I re--
- Oh, I know.

20:42.115 --> 20:44.284
So, tell me again, what's the plan?

20:46.119 --> 20:47.329
Knives or run.

20:49.748 --> 20:51.124
Okay, Crazy.

20:53.043 --> 20:54.044
Here we go.

21:21.280 --> 21:22.823
So far, so good.

21:29.454 --> 21:30.622
Wait.

21:34.293 --> 21:35.836
Do you hear something?

21:44.636 --> 21:45.637
No.

21:51.727 --> 21:53.270
So, this way then?

21:54.896 --> 21:55.897
Yeah.

22:25.135 --> 22:27.512
Lots of windows in here. Let's be careful.

22:30.182 --> 22:31.183
Okay.

22:53.330 --> 22:54.331
Dina.

23:10.764 --> 23:13.015
What the fuck is that?
And why is it hiding?

23:13.016 --> 23:14.975
I think it's a smart one,

23:14.976 --> 23:16.811
like the one that stalked me
at the supermarket.

23:16.812 --> 23:19.814
Okay, but you killed that one,
so we can kill this one too, right?

23:19.815 --> 23:22.400
Yes, I killed it. Not before it got me.

23:22.401 --> 23:24.527
- It fucking bit you?
- What was I supposed to do, tell you?

23:24.528 --> 23:25.987
You would've--

23:27.781 --> 23:29.657
Listen, if it's like the other one,

23:29.658 --> 23:31.700
it's gonna be fast
and it's gonna be sneaky.

23:31.701 --> 23:33.577
But this time, it's two on one.

23:33.578 --> 23:38.082
Now, that fucker's gonna try to flank us,
so I say we flank it first.

23:38.083 --> 23:41.127
We split up. Whichever one it follows,

23:41.128 --> 23:43.129
the other one comes up
and takes it out from behind.

23:43.130 --> 23:44.214
Plan?

23:47.050 --> 23:48.260
Plan.

24:02.190 --> 24:03.733
- What do we do?
- I don't know.

24:04.651 --> 24:05.902
Let's go back the way we came.

24:06.820 --> 24:09.072
If we run, they're gonna chase
so we have to go slow.

24:20.876 --> 24:23.502
You see that fencing over there?
I'm gonna lure as many as I can.

24:23.503 --> 24:25.004
You're gonna run in there,
secure the gate,

24:25.005 --> 24:26.506
secure it however you can,
and stay in there.

24:27.007 --> 24:30.552
Dina. I can get bit a lot.
You can't. Do as I say.

24:32.304 --> 24:33.305
Go!

25:47.379 --> 25:49.588
- Did you get bit?
- What? No.

25:49.589 --> 25:50.965
She's okay.

25:50.966 --> 25:53.385
I was watching. They didn't bite her.

25:54.219 --> 25:55.971
Jesse, I swear.

25:57.514 --> 25:58.515
We gotta go.

26:04.354 --> 26:05.564
Move! Move! Move!

26:06.523 --> 26:08.942
Don't stop! Keep going!

26:09.484 --> 26:10.776
I'll shoot 'em! Go!

26:10.777 --> 26:12.069
Heading west!

26:12.070 --> 26:13.738
Over there! Over there!

26:29.170 --> 26:32.215
The park!
We can lose 'em in there. Come on!

26:43.727 --> 26:45.936
Stop. Stop. We don't go in there.

26:45.937 --> 26:49.273
Looks like five, three unknowns,
chased into the park. Heavily armed.

26:49.274 --> 26:50.900
- Not Scars.
- What are they doing?

26:52.068 --> 26:54.320
If they try and come out, shoot 'em.

26:54.321 --> 26:55.696
Not coming in the park.

26:55.697 --> 26:57.781
You gotta be kidding me.

26:57.782 --> 26:59.950
Great. More infected.

26:59.951 --> 27:02.370
Maybe, but we can't go back that way.

27:03.872 --> 27:04.956
Come on.

27:09.377 --> 27:10.378
Jesse.

27:12.881 --> 27:13.922
Jesse.

27:13.923 --> 27:15.716
- What?
- How did you find us?

27:15.717 --> 27:17.802
The map you left in the theater.

27:18.887 --> 27:20.721
Impressive triangulation, by the way.

27:20.722 --> 27:21.889
Thanks, that was all Dina.

27:21.890 --> 27:23.432
Trust me, I didn't think it was you.

27:23.433 --> 27:24.892
How did you find the theater?

27:24.893 --> 27:26.811
Do I look like I wanna
fucking talk to you right now?

27:28.396 --> 27:29.938
You came alone?

27:29.939 --> 27:31.273
No. Me and Tommy.

27:31.274 --> 27:33.108
We split up when we got to the city.

27:33.109 --> 27:35.486
- Cover more ground.
- I can't believe they sent you after us.

27:35.487 --> 27:38.197
They didn't,
but you two were gonna die out here

27:38.198 --> 27:40.491
so we snuck out the next night.
And it's a good thing we did.

27:40.492 --> 27:41.867
You know what,
we were doing pretty fucking good

27:41.868 --> 27:43.411
- up until--
- Up until what?

27:47.666 --> 27:49.249
Until we weren't.

27:49.250 --> 27:51.168
Is Tommy okay?

27:51.169 --> 27:52.795
Hopefully.

27:52.796 --> 27:54.338
We're supposed to rendezvous
in the morning.

27:54.339 --> 27:56.882
- So, what now?
- Find a way out,

27:56.883 --> 27:58.593
get back to the theater,
shelter for the night.

27:59.094 --> 28:02.096
Meet up with Tommy,
and then we all go home.

28:02.097 --> 28:03.765
- No.
- Ellie.

28:09.354 --> 28:10.772
What the fuck is that?

28:30.041 --> 28:31.710
Hey. Go.

28:43.680 --> 28:46.473
No, wait, please. Please, please, please!

28:46.474 --> 28:48.517
I'm not like the others. Please.

28:48.518 --> 28:51.353
No, no, no, wait. Wait, wait, I'll join!

28:51.354 --> 28:53.313
- I'll join you. I'll join.
- Too late, Wolf.

28:53.314 --> 28:55.190
No, no. No, no, no, wait! I know things.

28:55.191 --> 28:57.277
I know what Isaac is planning.
I can help you. I can--

28:59.446 --> 29:01.739
We have no interest in your words.

29:01.740 --> 29:03.575
"For the corrupted soul knows only lies."

29:04.325 --> 29:05.492
So taught the Prophet.

29:05.493 --> 29:07.077
May She guide us.

29:07.078 --> 29:09.706
No. No. No. No. No.

29:12.167 --> 29:14.793
No. No, no, no.
Please, please, please. No.

29:14.794 --> 29:16.045
No. No.

29:16.880 --> 29:18.590
No! No! No!

29:20.175 --> 29:21.551
No.

29:30.435 --> 29:31.643
Oh, please, please, no.

29:31.644 --> 29:33.145
He is nested in sin.

29:33.146 --> 29:34.605
- No, no.
- Free him,

29:34.606 --> 29:37.065
that he may know Her love.

29:37.066 --> 29:38.859
No, no. No, no, no, no.

29:38.860 --> 29:40.570
Please, please, please, no.

30:00.340 --> 30:01.508
Now, he is free.

30:05.178 --> 30:06.930
Oh, fuck!

30:10.600 --> 30:12.309
I'll lead them away. Get her out. Go!

30:12.310 --> 30:14.312
I'll meet you back at the theater.
Fucking go!

30:17.106 --> 30:19.900
You won't get away, Wolf. She sees you.

30:19.901 --> 30:21.194
She watches over us all.

30:58.857 --> 31:00.024
He's not here.

31:05.154 --> 31:07.906
- May She guide us.
- May She guide us.

31:07.907 --> 31:10.493
Alright, spread out. Keep moving.

32:39.499 --> 32:41.083
What do we got?

32:41.084 --> 32:42.877
Not sure. Checking it out.

32:43.670 --> 32:44.963
Come on, Bonnie.

33:09.529 --> 33:11.238
It was a critter or something.

33:11.239 --> 33:12.657
All clear.

33:24.335 --> 33:25.545
You're all set.

34:08.963 --> 34:10.465
Put that shit down.

34:11.716 --> 34:13.551
Hands up. Turn around.

34:24.395 --> 34:25.521
You remember me?

34:26.856 --> 34:28.399
Yeah, you remember me.

34:29.817 --> 34:32.445
- What do you want?
- Where's Abby?

34:33.571 --> 34:35.947
- I don't know.
- Yes, you do.

34:35.948 --> 34:38.533
You shoot me, the sound will have
every soldier come running.

34:38.534 --> 34:40.036
You'll still be dead.

34:43.331 --> 34:45.291
Tell me where she is
and maybe I let you go.

34:47.210 --> 34:49.836
- We could've killed you.
- Maybe you should have.

34:49.837 --> 34:53.633
Or maybe you should've stayed the fuck
out of Jackson, Nora.

34:55.051 --> 34:56.177
Where's Abby?

35:05.061 --> 35:06.979
I'm sorry you saw it happen.

35:09.273 --> 35:11.566
No one should ever have to see
something like that.

35:11.567 --> 35:14.111
- Stop it.
- Sometimes at night,

35:14.112 --> 35:16.781
I still hear his screams.

35:17.824 --> 35:21.202
It was a terrible thing, the way he died.

35:22.453 --> 35:23.871
Yeah.

35:25.498 --> 35:27.542
Yeah, the little bitch
got what he deserved.

35:32.004 --> 35:33.464
Motherfucker!

35:34.382 --> 35:35.591
Intruder!

35:37.760 --> 35:38.761
Intruder!

35:40.388 --> 35:42.598
Hey! Shoot her!

36:01.450 --> 36:03.035
Oh, no, no, no, no.

36:04.328 --> 36:06.622
Nora, you're gonna fucking die!

36:08.082 --> 36:09.167
Nora!

36:37.445 --> 36:38.820
Fuck, it's open.

36:38.821 --> 36:40.447
The fucking shaft is open!

36:40.448 --> 36:42.992
- Seal off the hallway!
- Back, back, back!

36:44.493 --> 36:45.953
The shaft is open.

39:45.132 --> 39:46.967
You stupid bitch.

39:47.968 --> 39:49.261
Spores.

39:50.304 --> 39:52.515
We're breathing spores.

39:54.141 --> 39:55.267
We're infected.

39:56.268 --> 39:57.895
You killed us both.

39:58.979 --> 39:59.980
Did I?

40:12.076 --> 40:13.452
You're...

40:14.078 --> 40:15.413
You're her.

40:17.957 --> 40:19.875
The immune girl, you're...

40:20.584 --> 40:21.961
You're real.

40:24.505 --> 40:25.506
Yeah.

40:27.049 --> 40:28.634
Where's Abby?

40:32.304 --> 40:34.306
Don't you know what he did?

40:35.724 --> 40:38.644
- I don't care.
- You don't care?

40:40.896 --> 40:45.192
He killed everyone in that hospital.

40:46.819 --> 40:51.031
Including the only fucking person alive
that could make a cure from you.

40:54.368 --> 40:56.078
That was Abby's father.

40:57.872 --> 40:59.165
And Joel...

41:00.541 --> 41:03.377
Joel shot him in the head.

41:05.004 --> 41:06.881
That's what he did.

41:12.845 --> 41:14.472
I know.

41:36.202 --> 41:37.578
Where's Abby?

41:44.460 --> 41:45.461
No.

42:18.744 --> 42:20.412
Where is she?

42:24.833 --> 42:25.834
No.

42:33.717 --> 42:34.968
Where is she?

42:34.969 --> 42:36.178
No.

42:40.349 --> 42:41.725
Where is she?!

43:10.212 --> 43:11.463
Hey, kiddo.

43:15.301 --> 43:16.302
Hi.
